dby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T08:26:36-08:00","id":417563,"title":"","content":"over here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...OazOW1Mg/edit#</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T08:30:47-08:00","id":417569,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about &quot;best&quot; Charms but one of the goals of TAW was to make Lunar Charms thematically unique and flavorful in a way that the 2e RAW &quot;Silver Solar&quot; Charms largely were not. So for that alone I'd say they're &quot;better&quot; because they represent a specifically-defined and implemented Lunar aesthetic, where the RAW Charms don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T11:08:30-08:00","id":417699,"title":"","content":"IIRC, RAW Lunars are the better shapeshifters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:03:28-08:00","id":417754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiwuno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw#post417202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey all its your (least) favorite newbie again. So I recently downloaded a copy of Terrifying Argent witches and have been comparing them with the core Lunars and can see why people like this fan work so much. Unfortunately I have yet to have the opportunity to run either version of the splat and I was wondering. What are some of the major difference between the two in terms of both theme and overall abilities? Who are the better shifters? Who have the most available form options? Who as the &quot;best&quot; charms. This is mostly just an opinion question to sate my own curiosity but I would like to hear the fanbases thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Canon Lunars are silver Solars. TAW Lunars are silver Infernals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:11:09-08:00","id":417761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=417754#post417754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Canon Lunars are silver Solars. TAW Lunars are silver Infernals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've heard Silver Sidereals in reference to them as well.<br /> <br /> Me, they kind struck me as wee bit Abyssal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:16:29-08:00","id":417767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=417761#post417761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've heard Silver Sidereals in reference to them as well.<br /> <br /> Me, they kind struck me as wee bit Abyssal.</div> </div> </div> </div>There seems to be widespread agreement that whatever they are, they aren't really very Lunar at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:40:56-08:00","id":417798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=417767#post417767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There seems to be widespread agreement that whatever they are, they aren't really very Lunar at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, of course, is funny, because we agree that canon Lunars aren't Lunar enough, but we can't agree on what Lunars should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:46:46-08:00","id":417803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=417798#post417798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which, of course, is funny, because we agree that canon Lunars aren't Lunar enough, but we can't agree on what Lunars should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e made a lot of craaaaaazy promises in order to distance itself from 1e. It's thrown things off quite far from &quot;bestial shapeshifters in a savage setting&quot;, which was the original core concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:28:05-08:00","id":417886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=417803#post417803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's thrown things off quite far from &quot;bestial shapeshifters in a savage setting&quot;, which was the original core concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>And which [/i]also[/i] drew a lot of criticism for being one-dimensional savage &quot;barbarism yay!&quot; brutes who never really achived anything. So, again, most people agree that they don't want those Lunars either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:34:13-08:00","id":417897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=417886#post417886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And which [/i]also[/i] drew a lot of criticism for being one-dimensional savage &quot;barbarism yay!&quot; brutes who never really achived anything. So, again, most people agree that they don't want those Lunars either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Savage barbarism had a lot of potential, but the Storytelling chapter really dropped the ball (&quot;differentiate your characters based on their weapons - Sword Guy, Axe Guy, etc.&quot;). That, paired with making people care about a splat that inherently rejects civilization (i.e. where all the Stuff is happening in the setting and where most of the other splats exist and grind against each other for supremacy) in favor of being on the edges of the world (i.e. where basically nothing is happening unless you make it happen).<br /> <br /> Really the latter is the worst thing one can do when trying to present a splat that should have ongoing important deeds under its belt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:35:53-08:00","id":417903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=417886#post417886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And which [/i]also[/i] drew a lot of criticism for being one-dimensional savage &quot;barbarism yay!&quot; brutes who never really achived anything. So, again, most people agree that they don't want those Lunars either.</div> </div> </div> </div>The core concept wasn't the problem. The execution was left lacking by, from what we've heard, <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/troubled-lunar-history\" target=\"_blank\">hiring people who hated the concept, treating it with disdain, and injecting something else.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:45:50-08:00","id":417922,"title":"","content":"Heh. Sorry, my Lunar version history isn't that detailed. The important part still stands: Every published Lunar version so far was found lacking, for different reasons each time. And they're still a splat that inspires people enough that &quot;every thread is a Lunar thread&quot; has become a meme. (&quot;A forum thread either dies on-topic, or lives to become a Lunar thread&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:48:27-08:00","id":417927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=417922#post417922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they're still a splat that inspires people enough that &quot;every thread is a Lunar thread&quot; has become a meme. (&quot;A forum thread either dies on-topic, or lives to become a Lunar thread&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>We Lunar fans are an insatiable virus, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:33:37-08:00","id":417973,"title":"","content":"Well personally I and at least one other of my players have grown to love the Lunars. Their nature as shapeshifters with such a wide range of options available to them allows for some very fun possibilites in games. That said I can understand, i think the dislike that the fan base has for them always being encouraged to live on the edge of the world when so many fun ideas can be had with them in urban or at least civilized parts of the world. I also see the sideral comparrison in TAW espically that one charm tree that lets you pick pocket internal organs among others. I also find the TAW characterizations to be very interesting and evocative I espically like the write up for Ma-Ha-Suchi as this mad brilliant social engineer slowly trying to bleed civilization dry with ever more harsh and crippling papercuts. Its much more interesting (to me) than the barbarian who wants to break your cities just cause version that I see in the RAW. That said Characterization is characterization and I believe I am free to use what ever version of him I like in my games correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2107-wiwuno","name":"Wiwuno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:59:36-08:00","id":418014,"title":"","content":"Basically, while TAW does some cool things and is certainly better in many ways than canonical 2e Lunars, in many ways it focuses too much on the ...weird part of Luna, I suppose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T15:50:30-08:00","id":418051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Basically, while TAW does some cool things and is certainly better in many ways than canonical 2e Lunars, in many ways it focuses too much on the ...weird part of Luna, I suppose?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly on the aspects she gained from Othermoons over the traits she herself has, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiwuno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=417973#post417973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well personally I and at least one other of my players have grown to love the Lunars. Their nature as shapeshifters with such a wide range of options available to them allows for some very fun possibilites in games. That said I can understand, i think the dislike that the fan base has for them always being encouraged to live on the edge of the world when so many fun ideas can be had with them in urban or at least civilized parts of the world. I also see the sideral comparrison in TAW espically that one charm tree that lets you pick pocket internal organs among others. I also find the TAW characterizations to be very interesting and evocative I espically like the write up for Ma-Ha-Suchi as this mad brilliant social engineer slowly trying to bleed civilization dry with ever more harsh and crippling papercuts. Its much more interesting (to me) than the barbarian who wants to break your cities just cause version that I see in the RAW. That said Characterization is characterization and I believe I am free to use what ever version of him I like in my games correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some Lunars that should be into the slow bleed while pulling on invisible strings, but Ma-Ha-Suchi has always been the sort that wants to think bigger, and his approach has always been direct. In the original 1e writeup, he has his eyes on the Scavenger Lands to act as a base of operations before assaulting the Blessed Isle, He isn't driving the Arczekh hordes into the River Province because he wants to see the world burn.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the 2e writeup of MHS wins some kind of negative award for how much worse it became than the original. The Rutting Pens, the obsessive need to make Lunars completely broken monsters of WH40K's version of chaos, the whimsical Meatloaf references... that's a mess that can only be remedied with copious amounts of fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T17:10:13-08:00","id":418109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=417767#post417767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There seems to be widespread agreement that whatever they are, they aren't really very Lunar at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I'm still a fan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T18:09:19-08:00","id":418158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=417754#post417754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Canon Lunars are silver Solars. TAW Lunars are silver Infernals.</div> </div> </div> </div>so damned sick of that comparison.<br /> <br /> No, TAW's are not 'Silver Infernals', especially not the revised version. Having Charms that follow thematic trees rather than strict, straightforward mechanical progression is not unusual in Exalted; if anything, it's Solars who are unusual in building so much of their charmset around the latter. Yes, the original TAW's had some effects copied from Infernals. Infernals were the best-built rules in town at the time, and TAW had 400 Charms back then, mostly written by two people. Of course some of them were lazier jobs than others.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> That out of the way, yes, TAW's focus more on the weirder aspects of Luna. For my part, I think that's a good thing. I think pigeonholing Lunars as barbarian werewolves is shallow and limiting, because it reflects only a tiny part of lunar (small l) mythology.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say that barbarian werewolves isn't a thing Lunars should be able to do, and TAW's can do that, but if you look into the mythology of the moon and figures associated with it (example; Tezcatlipoca, the Smoking Mirror, Enemy of Both Sides, Lord of the Near and Far), they usually go to a lot of weird and wonderful places. Focusing on that also lets you build a more effective contrast with Solars, because once you're delving into the weirder myths it's a small step to things like Dionysus, and then you've got the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollonian_and_Dionysian\" target=\"_blank\">Apollonian/Dionysian contrast.</a> Mythology is full of this stuff that's absolutely <i>ripe</i> for Lunar inspiration. Seriously, I have <i>nine pages</i> of reference material for TAW inspiration as part of a supplement I'm working on, and I didn't even look that hard. Passing all that over to focus on barbarian werewolves and only barbarian werewolves seems almost criminally small-minded to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 02-24-2015, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T18:33:28-08:00","id":418176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418158#post418158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so damned sick of that comparison.<br /> <br /> No, TAW's are not 'Silver Infernals', especially not the revised version. Having Charms that follow thematic trees rather than strict, straightforward mechanical progression is not unusual in Exalted; if anything, it's Solars who are unusual in building so much of their charmset around the latter. Yes, the original TAW's had some effects copied from Infernals. Infernals were the best-built rules in town at the time, and TAW had 400 Charms back then, mostly written by two people. Of course some of them were lazier jobs than others.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> That out of the way, yes, TAW's focus more on the weirder aspects of Luna. For my part, I think that's a good thing. I think pigeonholing Lunars as barbarian werewolves is shallow and limiting, because it reflects only a tiny part of lunar (small l) mythology.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say that barbarian werewolves isn't a thing Lunars should be able to do, but if you look into the mythology of the moon and figures associated with it (example; Tezcatlipoca, the Smoking Mirror, Enemy of Both Sides, Lord of the Near and Far), they usually go to a lot of weird and wonderful places. Focusing on that also lets you build a more effective contrast with Solars, because once you're delving into the weirder myths it's a small step to things like Dionysus, and then you've got the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollonian_and_Dionysian\" target=\"_blank\">Apollonian/Dionysian contrast.</a> Mythology is full of this stuff that's absolutely <i>ripe</i> for Lunar inspiration. Seriously, I have <i>nine pages</i> of reference material for TAW inspiration as part of a supplement I'm working on, and I didn't even look that hard. Passing all that over to focus on barbarian werewolves and only barbarian werewolves seems almost criminally small-minded to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now me, I just think they're cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T19:20:15-08:00","id":418210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418176#post418176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now me, I just think they're cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, totes. I've just been working on and with TAW's for long enough and closely enough that I go into more detail when articulating <i>why</i> I think they're cool.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T21:18:20-08:00","id":418365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418158#post418158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Passing all that over to focus on barbarian werewolves and only barbarian werewolves seems almost criminally small-minded to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Holden has mentioned other shapeshifter myths out there. I remember a quote about were-hyenas or something from Africa. I suspect they are tapping just as large a vein of inspiration as the less well known moon myths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T21:53:50-08:00","id":418405,"title":"","content":"Wow. I have really needed for a while now an answer to &quot;what happens if the Yozis get ahold of a Lunar essence&quot;, for a campaign I am preparing to run.<br /> <br /> All I can say is, YOINK.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Murcushio: Sure, you avoid all that messy withdrawal, but you still need to <i>stop doing heroin</i> (for the purposes of this discussion your cousin is named Heroin).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4657-maxastro","name":"MaxAstro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T22:44:47-08:00","id":418434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418365#post418365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, Holden has mentioned other shapeshifter myths out there. I remember a quote about were-hyenas or something from Africa. I suspect they are tapping just as large a vein of inspiration as the less well known moon myths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the quote in question:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Werewolf-inspired Exalted&quot; is arguably an even richer concept-mine than &quot;Frankenstein-inspired Exalted.&quot;[1] [...]<br /> <br /> [1] Particularly when you expand &quot;Frankenstein&quot; to &quot;all tales of created life or unnatural outcasts are fair game for inspiration,&quot; and particularly when you expand &quot;werewolf&quot; to &quot;all tales of bestial dualism, and all shapeshifting folklore of any kind.&quot; I mean, hardly anyone in America has ever even heard of them, but I could riff on African werehyena legends alone pretty much forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T03:21:09-08:00","id":418558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=417922#post417922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh. Sorry, my Lunar version history isn't that detailed. The important part still stands: Every published Lunar version so far was found lacking, for different reasons each time. And they're still a splat that inspires people enough that &quot;every thread is a Lunar thread&quot; has become a meme. (&quot;A forum thread either dies on-topic, or lives to become a Lunar thread&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Other Exalted types have had at least one generally accepted execution that gives some common ground for discussion, even if 3E is moving away from it (like with Infernals). Lunars are in the weird place where nobody is really happy with either version of what they <i>are</i>, everyone agrees they <i>could</i> be awesome, but nobody seems able to agree on <i>how</i> that should be done. So there isn't one single part of the original presentation of Lunars that someone hasn't argued should be jettisoned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T05:12:30-08:00","id":418603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418365#post418365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Holden has mentioned other shapeshifter myths out there. I remember a quote about were-hyenas or something from Africa. I suspect they are tapping just as large a vein of inspiration as the less well known moon myths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure! But, even when you generalize 'werewolves' into therianthropes as a whole, that's still leaving out a bunch of other shapeshifting lore and popular culture, like the birth-myth of Taliesin, the exploits of Loki, the varied aspects of Tezcatlipoca, the yee naaldlooshi of Navajo myth, Sun Wukong out of China, Mystique and Beast Boy from comics, Bayonetta... Then you get the various patchwork monsters that aren't shapeshifters, like Chimera or the Chinese Nue, or heroes of inhuman, magical origins like Lancelot, or Claymores and Witchers...<br /> <br /> Holden is quite correct that there's more to 'werewolf' folklore than were<i>wolves</i>, but you can't really generalize 'werewolves' to 'all shapeshifting lore', because so many shapeshifting stories are tied up in entirely different paradigms. Even if you could, that's still passing over a wealth of mythological creatures and figures who either aren't shapeshifters or aren't<i> defined by being</i> shapeshifters, but who are still excellent Lunar material. I mean heck, <a href=\"http://scans-daily.dreamwidth.org/4786981.html#cutid1\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Moon Knight</i>,</a> man!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 02-25-2015, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T05:23:04-08:00","id":418617,"title":"","content":"Lunars are not Mystique for a reason, though - by broadening the definition of &quot;shapeshifter&quot; to <i>that</i> broad a degree, you get an incoherent mess - which is what we don't want for a third time in a row.<br /> <br /> Imagine if Sidereals drew on <i>every</i> myth related to the concept of Heaven - the angelic Abrahamic stuff would clash pretty damned hard with the Chinese bureaucracy heaven, and readers wouldn't know <i>what</i> to make of it.<br /> <br /> Or if the fluff of Malfeas included every instance of demons from pop culture - I shudder to think of what <i>that</i> shitpile would look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-19-2020, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T06:39:21-08:00","id":418653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418617#post418617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars are not Mystique for a reason, though - by broadening the definition of &quot;shapeshifter&quot; to <i>that</i> broad a degree, you get an incoherent mess - which is what we don't want for a third time in a row.<br /> <br /> Imagine if Sidereals drew on <i>every</i> myth related to the concept of Heaven - the angelic Judeo-Christian stuff would clash pretty damned hard with the Chinese bureaucracy heaven, and readers wouldn't know <i>what</i> to make of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, first off, the stuff Mystique does is the sort of thing you can easily replicate with Solar Larceny. I <i>seriously</i> disagree with the idea that having Lunar shapeshifting being able to represent that is at all onerous.<br /> <br /> Second, Sidereals <i>don't</i> draw on myths related to the concept of heaven. Or at least, their magic doesn't. Sidereals are fatespinners, prophets and puppetmasters, not the Heaven Exalted. Heaven is where they live, not who they are.<br /> <br /> But even if Sidereals <i>were </i>the Heaven Exalted, I disagree that dra<span style=\"font-size:14px\">wing on every myth related to the idea of Heaven would necessarily make an incoherent mess. That kind of incoherence doesn't happen just by drawing on different myths - drawing on different sources is a <i>good</i> thing, when it's done intelligently. A wide array of sources is a large part, for example, of why Tolkien's work has endured for so long;<span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> he had a deep knowledge of North European myth, epic, and folklore, which he filtered through Roman Catholic theology, which he also knew a fair bit about, and his own literary skill and imagination.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Incoherence, at least to me, is a product of trying to maintain clashing <i>elements</i> of disparate sources without resolving them, not simply drawing on a wide array of sources to begin with. It's a large part of why Exalted itself is such a compelling setting for me, <i>because </i>it draws on so many different areas of history and mythology and, for the most, harmonizes them. Witness SLS talking about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/66510-if-you-want-to-understand-exalted?p=85274#post85274\">the four levels</a> that Exalted operates on in his thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 02-26-2015, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T06:52:50-08:00","id":418664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418653#post418653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, first off, the stuff Mystique does is the sort of thing you can easily replicate with Solar Larceny.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026depending on the version of Mystique, perhaps.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I <i>seriously</i> disagree with the idea that having Lunar shapeshifting being able to represent that is at all onerous. </div> </div> </div>We've already been told in no uncertain terms that Lunars will not be Mystique <i>or</i> Alex Mercer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, Sidereals <i>don't</i> draw on myths related to the concept of heaven. Or at least, their magic doesn't. </div> </div> </div>Except where it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heaven is where they live, not who they are. </div> </div> </div>Except when it is who they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:20:38-08:00","id":418694,"title":"","content":"The TAW Project - in many ways it is the zenith of that whole Infernals focused fandom from that time of 2e. And Revlid is actually a good writer! He managed to make a lot of 2e and late 2e ideas exciting (which is hard to do). If 3e were about continuing late 2e's vision...<br /> <br /> For the TAW themselves, my impression of them has always been (and this is with the disclaimer I'm not a head who has read them a lot)...<br /> <br /> They're pretty much what their name says they are :<br /> <br /> - Terrifying - their magic sows terror and provokes fear, they unsettle, they trouble, they predate - they can use this to coerce and control humanity<br /> <br /> - Witches - they feel witches in the Western tradition, which are made distinct from sorcerers and wizards in they invoke magic which is decidedly irrational, bloodied, earthy, from the natural world, rooted in sacrifice and bad luck, unsettling, does not really feel &quot;clean&quot;.<br /> <br /> (And I guess they're argent in that they're also somehow shiny?)<br /> <br /> Your mileage with the TAW as a concept will depend on how interesting you find these two main aspects together. Do you want to be terrifying and work through terror? Do you want to wield magic that feels like witches' magic?<br /> <br /> Yes, they clearly come from the parts of the fandom who were overwhelmingly in love with Infernals - particularly with those ideas where you are a person who has the challenge of using morally tainting and inhumane for ends which are moral or humane. It is a dark vision.<br /> <br /> I don't have much interest in any of that stuff, really! (For instance, I'm not interested in people who use terrorist tactics &quot;for good&quot;).<br /> <br /> (I also have a slight distaste for the way TAW seems to use comparatively large amounts of complex mythology from their god to yield comparatively small levels of interesting magic, seems uneconomical - many more splats seem to get a lot out of beginning with a comparatively small amount of ideas. This is also true of Infernals).<br /> <br /> Your mileage will vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:22:32-08:00","id":418695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418664#post418664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've already been told in no uncertain terms that Lunars will not be Mystique <i>or</i> Alex Mercer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes? What's your point? I know what the devs are doing with Lunars; I have, from the start, been quite clearly talking about how I <i>disagree</i> with that direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except where it does.<br /> Except when it is who they are. </div> </div> </div>Such as? What do Sidereals <i>do</i> that's Heavenly? I suppose they're tied into the Celestial Bureaucracy coming as it does from Chinese Mythology, but really, paperwork is hardly the foremost thing about Sidereals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418694#post418694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the TAW themselves, my impression of them has always been (and this is with the disclaimer I'm not a head who has read them a lot)...</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm, that's fair enough. I still heavily contest the 'Silver Infernals' idea (&quot;Using morally tainted and inhumane ends to good purposes&quot; is an idea that was around long before Infernals), and I'd point out that while TAW powers do encourage a bloody, guerilla warfare approach to problems, the material also acknowledges the knife-edge this kind of thing walks.<br /> <br /> That aside, you're pretty much on point. TAW's have always worked towards a specific vision, and it's not for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 02-25-2015, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:35:23-08:00","id":418712,"title":"","content":"Hey, folks, raise your hand if you've played a RAW, Ronin Sidereal! No one? How about you, <i>way</i> in the back? You? Okay, so only like two people ever have played Ronin Sidereals, I'd say that's a pretty good indicator that being part of the bureaucracy of Heaven is (relatively) central to their identity.<br /> <br /> Okay, with that out of the way, they interact with the gods of heaven, including the various departments, bureaus, conventions, and offices of which they are part (it's not all a matter of paperwork and you know it); they get paid in the coin of Heaven, participate in the politics of the Celestial City, and even use it as a shortcut to get from place to place quickly; they use their potent magics to call up gods and elementals, sanction spirits, lay curses into the stars themselves, and check the plans of the gods.<br /> <br /> As a matter of fact, there <i>is</i> some overlap between &quot;Agents of Heaven&quot; and the whole fatespinner schtick you're pushing, but <i>the Loom of Fate is <b>in</b> Heaven</i>, as are all the coworkers in the vast bureaucracy of which they are part. The time they spend up there shapes them just as much as the magics they learn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-25-2015, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:57:11-08:00","id":418732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418712#post418712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, with that out of the way, they interact with the gods of heaven, including the various departments, bureaus, conventions, and offices of which they are part (it's not all a matter of paperwork and you know it); they get paid in the coin of Heaven, participate in the politics of the Celestial City, and even use it as a shortcut to get from place to place quickly; they use their potent magics to call up gods and elementals, sanction spirits, lay curses into the stars themselves, and check the plans of the gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I acknowledged as much to begin with. Heaven is <i>where Sidereals live</i>, but it has very little to do with <i>who Sidereals are</i>. In the setting of Exalted, individual Sidereals live in Heaven and are shaped by its lifestyle and politics. But the nature of Sidereals, the essence of what makes them a Sidereal, does not draw on Heavenly lore; Sidereals are not angelic figures of salvation, nor do they draw on the eternal, undying feasting and battle of the Einherjar, or the personalized paradise of the Elysian Fields. Heaven's Reach turned 'Heaven' into a giant computer library without meaningfully changing the nature of Sidereals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a matter of fact, there <i>is</i> some overlap between &quot;Heaven&quot; and the whole fatespinner schtick you're pushing, but <i>the Loom of Fate is <b>in</b> Heaven</i>, as are all the coworkers in the vast bureaucracy of which they are part. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's a setting conceit, not tied into heavenly lore. Sidereals' connection to Fate is routed through their association with the stars, and therefore astrology and destiny. For their association with destiny (as represented by the Loom) to be Heavenly, it would probably need to work more along the lines of an Abrahamic tradition, where divinities are planners who run the world, rather than bureaucrats who record and maintain the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 02-25-2015, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T08:10:39-08:00","id":418743,"title":"","content":"&quot;Heaven&quot; in Exalted is more analogous to Mount Olympus, with a lot of asshole gods sitting around, pushing humans into taking courses of actions. It also draws fairly heavily from Asian (Chinese, Tibetan, Japanese and Hindu) mythology about Heaven. It doesn't really draw much on the Abrahamic concept of Heaven, as this place souls go to when they die. You'll note in those earlier religions, souls don't go to heaven when they die - in fact for the most people, people don't go there much at all.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for undying feasting halls and battlefields or the Elysian Fields you'd be better off looking at the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T08:20:24-08:00","id":418748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418732#post418732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I acknowledged as much to begin with. Heaven is <i>where Sidereals live</i>, but it has very little to do with <i>who Sidereals are</i>. In the setting of Exalted, individual Sidereals live in Heaven and are shaped by its lifestyle and politics. But the nature of Sidereals, the essence of what makes them a Sidereal, does not draw on Heavenly lore; Sidereals are not angelic figures of salvation, nor do they draw on the eternal, undying feasting and battle of the Einherjar, or the personalized paradise of the Elysian Fields. Heaven's Reach turned 'Heaven' into a giant computer library without meaningfully changing the nature of Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Yes, but that's a setting conceit, not tied into heavenly lore. Sidereals' connection to Fate is routed through their association with the stars, and therefore astrology and destiny. For their association with destiny (as represented by the Loom) to be Heavenly, it would probably need to work more along the lines of an Abrahamic tradition, where divinities are planners who run the world, rather than bureaucrats who record and maintain the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creation's Heavenly city of Yu-Shan is, as the name would suggest, based more on Chinese traditional ideas of Heaven, which was defined by being a bureacracy. If you ever watch Chinese wuxia fantasy, corrupt bureaucrats in Heaven as the enemies are a common theme.<br /> Hell too is also a bureaucracy, hence the story where Sun Wukong erases his monkey's names from the ledgers so they can't die, because, well, they're not in the bureaucracy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T08:28:59-08:00","id":418772,"title":"","content":"At this point I can't help but be suspicious of the idea that you aren't being deliberately obtuse here - the Sidereals <i>do</i> very much draw inspiration from Heaven, <i>but just the Chinese one</i>. They aren't Abrahamic angels because they're too busy being Great Sage Erlang or Bodhisattva Guanyin. Trying to shoehorn in the Abrahamic heaven into their theme would only dilute the themes presented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-25-2015, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T08:36:14-08:00","id":418780,"title":"","content":"Mmyup. If you were to say that office politics and bureaucracy shapes who Sidereals are (which is, I would point out, not <i>quite</i> the same thing as their place in the setting, although the two are connected), I would agree that it plays a part. That's represented in Chinese myth as Heaven, but it's also a thing in itself.<br /> <br /> See, there's a couple of layers of separation at work here, from my perspective. &quot;Who Sidereals are&quot; is Wise Heroes; figures of experience and knowledge who work behind the scenes and never (seem to) put a foot wrong. For example, take Avoidance Kata. Sidereals don't have Avoidance Kata because they have any particular association with teleportation or retcons, rather they have it because the Wise Hero never gets into a fight they cannot win, unless by losing they advance their cause.<br /> <br /> This is represented in Exalted with their ties to Destiny and Fate, which is in turn represented by the Loom, the engine of reality, which loops back around to Sidereals having powers like Avoidance Kata. Heaven is not who Sidereals are; it is the method of <i>realising</i> who Sidereals are.<br /> <br /> Also, fun fact; I'm pretty sure this is the <i>second</i> time I've seen a Lunar thread mutate into a Sidereal thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418772#post418772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point I can't help but be suspicious of the idea that you aren't being deliberately obtuse here - the Sidereals <i>do</i> very much draw inspiration from Heaven, <i>but just the Chinese one</i>. They aren't Abrahamic angels because they're too busy being Great Sage Erlang or Bodhisattva Guanyin. Trying to shoehorn in the Abrahamic heaven into their theme would only dilute the themes presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I say they aren't the Heaven Exalted, because remember back when I was talking about how drawing on a diverse array of sources is a <i>good</i> thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 02-25-2015, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T09:07:16-08:00","id":418804,"title":"","content":"A Lunars thread morphing into a Sids thread instead of the other way around? Madness!<br /> <br /> Corollary to the Rule that All Threads Become Lunars Threads: All Lunars Threads Include Arguments About Appropriateness of Alex Mercer as a Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T09:10:18-08:00","id":418810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418804#post418804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" cla