 a decade and a half ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T12:46:46-08:00","id":419199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418848#post418848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dont forget the &quot;All Lunar threads end up with a discussion of beast man and the morality of bestiality&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, if we're talking about that, can we get a Dragon King in here?<br /> Maybe with a little mortal assistance, their souls <i>are</i> replicable.<br /> <br /> Depends on if the result is more like a beastman or godblood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T13:43:32-08:00","id":419286,"title":"","content":"Damn, I forgot about parrots.<br /> <br /> I need more stringent guidelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T15:03:48-08:00","id":419366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MaxAstro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418405#post418405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. I have really needed for a while now an answer to &quot;what happens if the Yozis get ahold of a Lunar essence&quot;, for a campaign I am preparing to run.<br /> <br /> All I can say is, YOINK.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the last TAW Threads I remember reading was the Artimedean Exalted, a homebrew splat that served the Primordials (Because that's the sort of thing people encouraged at that time) in Gunstar Autochtonia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:28:25-08:00","id":419608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=419154#post419154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghastly beat everyone to it over a decade and a half ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here I thought I was the only one\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T19:10:14-08:00","id":419729,"title":"","content":"Back to TAW, I liked the Warden keyword. It was similar yet different enough from the Holy keyword to be interesting.<br /> <br /> Edit: Although, going back, apparently Creatures Of Death count as Outsiders, which I though was silly, but I guess I just disagree on a metaphysical level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1252,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","user":"God_of_Awesome","date":". 02-25-2015, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T20:15:30-08:00","id":419769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=419729#post419729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to TAW, I liked the Warden keyword. It was similar yet different enough from the Holy keyword to be interesting.<br /> <br /> Edit: Although, going back, apparently Creatures Of Death count as Outsiders, which I though was silly, but I guess I just disagree on a metaphysical level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creatures of Death are creatures of the Underworld, and the underworld...isn't Creation.<br /> It's a twisted mirror of Creation, but it isn't Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T21:13:42-08:00","id":419793,"title":"","content":"I always viewed it as native to Creation the same way a cancer was native to the body.<br /> <br /> Malfeas may have been cast out, excised, but the way I see the Neverborn dug themselves in deep into the natural order like some kind of parasite.<br /> <br /> But that's just me buttin' headcanons.<br /> <br /> Edit: On the other hand, way I see it, ol' Auto excised himself and anything Autochthonian would be considered an Outsider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T21:50:24-08:00","id":419837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=419793#post419793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always viewed it as native to Creation the same way a cancer was native to the body.<br /> <br /> Malfeas may have been cast out, excised, but the way I see the Neverborn dug themselves in deep into the natural order like some kind of parasite.<br /> <br /> But that's just me buttin' headcanons.<br /> <br /> Edit: On the other hand, way I see it, ol' Auto excised himself and anything Autochthonian would be considered an Outsider.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like that bit of headcanon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> About TAW Lunars, it's the first time i ever saw them, so i'm going to take some time to read them and see what i can exploit.<br /> If they don't fit my personal image of what Lunars should or not be i can always to explore stuff like the other Lunars, Chimerism, corruption of Lunar sparks by Yozis or Neverborn and a bunch of other alternatives, depending on what catches my fancy, same way my group has been thinking of keeping 2e Infernals in our future games by simply making them the creations of <b>another</b> Yozi clique or some such... win-win either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T08:37:12-08:00","id":420256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418780#post418780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why I say they aren't the Heaven Exalted, because remember back when I was talking about how drawing on a diverse array of sources is a <i>good</i> thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only up to a certain point. If you try to grab from everything you could conceivably grab from you're gonna end up with a mess, <i>especially</i> with something that pulls in as many diverse directions as shapeshifters. One of the smartest things Geoff did in the 1e Lunars outline was attaching a separate file to the effect of &quot;Okay, before anyone starts writing, we all need to be on the same page about how Lunar shapeshifting works and what kind of shapeshifters Lunars are, because otherwise you're all going to run off with a bunch of contradictory ideas and assumptions and I will have a mess on my hands. Lunar shapeshifting is like this......&quot; <br /> <br /> (The 2e outline, notably, did not have any such thing-- and what followed was 8 years of people arguing about what kind of shapeshifters Lunars are.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T08:40:08-08:00","id":420264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420256#post420256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">8 years of people arguing about what kind of shapeshifters Lunars are</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this year factored into that number?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T09:58:55-08:00","id":420397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420264#post420264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this year factored into that number?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, considering that we <i>are</i> arguing over what kind of shapeshifters Lunars are.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T11:05:00-08:00","id":420452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nervaqus987</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420397#post420397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, considering that we <i>are</i> arguing over what kind of shapeshifters Lunars are.....</div> </div> </div> </div>And the anniversary is in April, so after that, it will start on nine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T11:18:07-08:00","id":420461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420256#post420256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only up to a certain point. If you try to grab from everything you could conceivably grab from you're gonna end up with a mess, <i>especially</i> with something that pulls in as many diverse directions as shapeshifters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted. I would tend to view that point as varying, depending on the number of sources vs the authors ability to resolve conflicts between them. Part of the writers craft.<br /> <br /> Mind, on this point I prefer to sidestep the matter and found Lunars in Witchey, with shapeshifting as something they do rather than who they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 02-26-2015, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T12:58:25-08:00","id":420554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420461#post420461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind, on this point I prefer to sidestep the matter and found Lunars in Witchey, with shapeshifting as something they do rather than who they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which definitely makes them into not Lunars. The roots of Lunars are in Werewolf and shapeshifters are what werewolves are, rather than what they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T12:59:50-08:00","id":420555,"title":"","content":"Seeing these threads always made me want to write a remake of Solars called Terrific Aurulent Wizards.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Terrific Aurulent Wizards illuminate what that-which-is with the photolight of their burning souls. Focusing his inner photolight on a thing-that-is in the world around him, the Aurulent Wizard dispels the dread darkness surrounding it and exposes it to his all-seeing eyes. Then, guided by this vision, the Aurulent Wizard strikes, attempting to condemn a Thing-Which-Is into the Not through the universal language of physical violence.&quot;<br /> <br /> (The charm adds damage to a melee attack!)<br /> <br /> Gold is the new Silver. Solars are Golden Lunars now!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-26-2015, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T13:01:24-08:00","id":420556,"title":"","content":"I wonder if TAW is a good enough mock-up for Lunars while waiting for the 3e Lunars book.<br /> <br /> Certainly kinda fits the view of Lunars that Immaculates preach agains and the place of Lunars acting as guerrilla monsters raising up groups against the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 02-26-2015, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T13:16:31-08:00","id":420564,"title":"","content":"I liked the implication that TAW Lunars were the Solar's superior during the Primordial War, as they were simply better than them at tearing things down.<br /> <br /> But once everything was torn down and it was time to rebuild? Well, the Argent Witches had something to contribute, but this was the Solars' time to shine!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T13:18:54-08:00","id":420567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420461#post420461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted. I would tend to view that point as varying, depending on the number of sources vs the authors ability to resolve conflicts between them. Part of the writers craft.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not varying. That's like telling a professional chef that it's OK to pour every seasoning known to man into a single broth because taste varies, and that if he can't make a good soup out of that that he is some sort of lesser chef. If you served that bowl of soup you'd probably be put in jail for killing someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T13:20:24-08:00","id":420571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420567#post420567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not varying. That's like telling a professional chef that it's OK to pour every seasoning known to man into a single broth because taste varies, and that if he can't make a good soup out of that that he is some sort of lesser chef. If you served that bowl of soup you'd probably be put in jail for killing someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Craft: Thirteen Forbidden Spices Recipe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T13:22:44-08:00","id":420573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420564#post420564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the implication that TAW Lunars were the Solar's superior during the Primordial War, as they were simply better than them at tearing things down.<br /> <br /> But once everything was torn down and it was time to rebuild? Well, the Argent Witches had something to contribute, but this was the Solars' time to shine!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> what<br /> <br /> i<br /> i...i......i...........<br /> i<br /> <br /> what","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T13:26:00-08:00","id":420577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420573#post420573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> what<br /> <br /> i<br /> i...i......i...........<br /> i<br /> <br /> what</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5I5dfI4SyLg\" data-code=\"5I5dfI4SyLg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/5I5dfI4SyLg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T13:30:41-08:00","id":420585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420564#post420564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the implication that TAW Lunars were the Solar's superior during the Primordial War, as they were simply better than them at tearing things down.<br /> <br /> But once everything was torn down and it was time to rebuild? Well, the Argent Witches had something to contribute, but this was the Solars' time to shine!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you broke Holden.<br /> <br /> To be honest, it kind of makes a small bit of sense, but only if you squint -really- hard.<br /> Even then, the Solars would probably still be the 'superiors' anyway as far as military rank is concerned, as they would likely still be the ones in command, but the Lunars might have been the ones at the forefront of their armies. The Solars lead, and the Lunars champion their cause as the most indispensable weapon in their arsenal.<br /> Or something like that anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T14:05:05-08:00","id":420628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420585#post420585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you broke Holden.<br /> <br /> To be honest, it kind of makes a small bit of sense, but only if you squint -really- hard.<br /> Even then, the Solars would probably still be the 'superiors' anyway as far as military rank is concerned, as they would likely still be the ones in command, but the Lunars might have been the ones at the forefront of their armies. The Solars lead, and the Lunars champion their cause as the most indispensable weapon in their arsenal.<br /> Or something like that anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the past, we've sometimes discussed how if you take things the Solars are supposed to be good at and say &quot;but XYZ is universally better, because they're ultra-focused on it!&quot;, you end up turning Solars into jack-of-all-trades, master-of-none Exalted, which is certainly not what they're intended to be. This sometimes comes up when people say &quot;well, Lunars should be better at stealth or disguise&quot; or &quot;Alchemicals should be better at Craft&quot; or &quot;Sidereals should be better scholars.&quot;<br /> <br /> But this the first time I've seen someone put &quot;wrecking shit&quot; in that category.<br /> <br /> (Not really; people suggest it all the time for Abyssals.)<br /> <br /> Exalted's Exalt types aren't character classes. They're all intended to be complete and enough to approach the game on their own, especially Solars, without feeling like you're missing something important. I think that this cuts to the heart of what people are sometimes asking for when they compare types of Exalted and when they ask loaded questions like &quot;but was XYZ really <i>needed</i> in the Primordial War?&quot; Because what they're really asking -- the important question, anyway -- is &quot;are Lunars really needed to play the game? Do they serve a necessary role in a circle?&quot; And the answer to that is a definite and resounding no; that's not how the game is made at all. If you have a Lunar in your circle, it means that someone wants to tell a Lunar story, not that you needed them for some hypothetical Lunar Niche that only they can fill best, like a cleric in D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> Of course this is also true for everyone else; you don't need Solars in your circle unless you're aiming to tell Solar stories. But it's sort of an undercurrent I feel is present in a lot of the questions people ask about Lunars.<br /> <br /> (This is also part of why Lunars can't be absolutely everything, because you have to be able to answer &quot;what is a Lunar story?&quot; in some way -- it can be really really broad, but it needs a useful answer. And you have to answer it in a way which fits into the setting, which means &quot;be better than the Dawn at swording people&quot; can't be your story. You might <i>do</i> it, with an individual Lunar -- there's no rule saying the best swordsman in the world can't be a Lunar, though it might be an uphill fight -- but you can't give Lunars as a whole a core story incompatible with the Solar narrative like that, for the same reason you can't call absolutely everyone the Greatest Martial Artist Ever. The setting has to hold together as a whole, and some things people want don't work for that without eg. changing Solars.)<br /> <br /> I mean, while 3e seems to be giving them something, you wouldn't take &quot;Lunars breed beastmen&quot; and say that Lunars have used it to breed a mighty empire that is more powerful than the Realm; that would be dumb and wouldn't fit into the setting. Saying &quot;Lunars are simply better at murdering shit than Dawns, as part of the core definition of what a Lunar <i>is</i>&quot; runs into the same problem.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that aside, TAW does try to answer &quot;what is a Lunar story?&quot; to an extent... but I think that part of the reason people call them Silver Infernals is because they feel that that overarching story (even more than the individual charms) resembles the Infernal one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-26-2015, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T14:21:05-08:00","id":420668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420564#post420564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the implication that TAW Lunars were the Solar's superior during the Primordial War, as they were simply better than them at tearing things down.<br /> <br /> But once everything was torn down and it was time to rebuild? Well, the Argent Witches had something to contribute, but this was the Solars' time to shine!</div> </div> </div> </div>And people say Solar wank is out of control. If anything, Lunar fans need to tone it down a lot more....<br /> <br /> EDIT: On a side note, I suppose this confirms my suspicions that TAW are edging in to an outright mary sue splat, and wont be touching any of my games in any iteration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T15:00:09-08:00","id":420701,"title":"","content":"I didn't get that implication from my readings of that section, I was however left with the unmistakable impression that it was written by a Reclamation sympathiser though.<br /> The product is not without its faults but beating its chest and roaring &quot;better than Solars!&quot; is not one of them unless I'm really misremembering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-26-2015, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T15:08:04-08:00","id":420708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420554#post420554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which definitely makes them into not Lunars. The roots of Lunars are in Werewolf and shapeshifters are what werewolves are, rather than what they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Your point? I talked about that in my<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418158#post418158\"> first post in this thread</a>, man.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420567#post420567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not varying. That's like telling a professional chef that it's OK to pour every seasoning known to man into a single broth because taste varies, and that if he can't make a good soup out of that that he is some sort of lesser chef. If you served that bowl of soup you'd probably be put in jail for killing someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree that's an apt analogy, although I can see how you got that impression. Mea culpa.<br /> <br /> Although a certain amount of insight is involved, in that sometimes a good chef just knows that adding a pinch of this or that will make a dish even better, I would prefer to view it as a professional chef knowing how many seasonings can fit into one dish, and when they want to make larger dishes, or a larger spread of dishes, to accommodate more ingredients. The greater the feast, the more room there is for variety... If it can be carefully balanced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420585#post420585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you broke Holden.</div> </div> </div> </div>That broke <i>me</i> when I first read it, and I helped <i>write</i> TAW. I did a double-take when I saw that.<br /> <br /> Seriously, where the hell did that come from? TAW backstory doesn't compare Lunars and Solars much at all, honestly, I'm baffled where the idea that it implies they were better than Solars comes from, and I'm curious where God_of_Awesome got that idea.<br /> <br /> What I've always understood TAW's to be aiming for, and what I've tried to cleave to whenever I'm at the helm, is as people who are distinctly lagging behind in certain grand-scale areas like nation-shaping and crafting, in exchange for being just about equal to Solars in the arena of wrecking shit on a personal scale - which is a <i>huge freaking deal</i>, because equaling Solars at <i>anything</i> is a pretty big deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420628#post420628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, that aside, TAW does try to answer &quot;what is a Lunar story?&quot; to an extent... but I think that part of the reason people call them Silver Infernals is because they feel that that overarching story (even more than the individual charms) resembles the Infernal one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also curious about this, because I don't see it.<br /> <br /> The Infernal story in 2e, as I understand it, is heavily bound up in irrevocable transformation of the self and of rejecting the alien masters who recruited you with honeyed lies, then rolling around in Creation bending strange and disturbing cosmic power towards good ends.<br /> <br /> There's some overlap with TAW's there, yes, in that TAW's also deal in bending strange and frightening powers towards hopefully good ends, but that's hardly an Infernal only thing. Abyssal heroes have been doing it even longer, and heck, Sidereals would probably deal in it a lot more if their powers were less subtle. The notion of struggling with inhuman and not entirely benign power is a piece of storycraft with fairly deep roots, all told.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, TAW's don't have any alien masters to reject - their closest analogues would be the Deliberative-era elders, but those are written up as antagonists from the word go, and while TAW's do have a transformation angle, it's much more like putting on a new suit - it's a fluid, mercurial change that can be discarded, in contrast to the irreversible mutation of the self that Infernals deal in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 02-26-2015, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T15:17:11-08:00","id":420716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420708#post420708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree that's an apt analogy, although I can see how you got that impression. Mea culpa.</div> </div> </div> </div>That poor imprisoned cook also disagrees that you can ever pour &quot;too many&quot; spices into one broth. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T15:53:39-08:00","id":420758,"title":"","content":"All this talk of spices makes me think of TAW as whatever emerges when Van of the Dawn gets through <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qXOD0wVVXms\" target=\"_blank\">putting condiments on his food</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T15:58:08-08:00","id":420763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420668#post420668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And people say Solar wank is out of control. If anything, Lunar fans need to tone it down a lot more....</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah because it's soooooooo unreasonable that fans of a splat that's been narratively shit on for a decade and a half want better. Solars at least have consistently always had an important place in the setting history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420701#post420701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't get that implication from my readings of that section, I was however left with the unmistakable impression that it was written by a Reclamation sympathiser though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same. Though I don't really get the Infernal parallels all that much. Maybe that they're weird but it's not like Infernals have exclusive license on weird. TAW always struck me as thematically closer to Abyssals, but not narratively closer. If that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 02-26-2015, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T16:50:18-08:00","id":420836,"title":"","content":"Um, oops? Sorry Holden?<br /> <br /> Wait, why do you care about an opinion on TAW Lunars anywho?<br /> <br /> Nevermind.<br /> <br /> Basically, I meant something like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420585#post420585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you broke Holden.<br /> <br /> To be honest, it kind of makes a small bit of sense, but only if you squint -really- hard.<br /> Even then, the Solars would probably still be the 'superiors' anyway as far as military rank is concerned, as they would likely still be the ones in command, but the Lunars might have been the ones at the forefront of their armies. The Solars lead, and the Lunars champion their cause as the most indispensable weapon in their arsenal.<br /> Or something like that anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Minus the squinting. Solars lead, [TAW] Lunars destroyed. At least, my impression is that their charms had an entropic quality about it that even Abyssals don't have. They destroyed and tore things down and that's all they could do, hence why they couldn't replace the Solars after the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> This is all 2e, of course. 3e Lunars are, of course, going to be an entirely different and officially backed beast altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T16:51:20-08:00","id":420838,"title":"","content":"Narratively shat on...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T16:56:27-08:00","id":420842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420838#post420838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narratively shat on...?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think they meant the problem with the previous editions that I know you and John have observed yourself of Lunars having a lack of defined narrative role in history and metaphysics (how they could be dropped from the game entirely and nothing about the rest of the setting - save some secret backgrounds for a few countries - would change). From what we know about 3E changes this is something I'm confident there's a strong commitment to not repeat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T16:56:50-08:00","id":420843,"title":"","content":"Also, good Sol, I didn't actually expect people to have that wide a grade a response to what I said.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should end all my post with, &quot;And thus, such and such is better than Solars.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ya know, I wanna be an attention whore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T17:57:13-08:00","id":420908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420763#post420763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah because it's soooooooo unreasonable that fans of a splat that's been narratively shit on for a decade and a half want better. Solars at least have consistently always had an important place in the setting history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, I can understand how Lunar fans might feel that their favorite splat hasn't always gotten he best treatment. Heck, I can agree with it to some extent, and even go so far as to wish them the best of luck in the new edition.<br /> <br /> What I don't understand or sympathize with, is their incessant need to pollute the entire forum with Lunar threads, or turn every thread in to a Lunar thread, or bring up Lunars where they aren't even relevant to the discussion. I was, for the longest time, completely indifferent towards Lunars. I didn't dislike them, but they never appealed to me in any way like Sidereal, Infernals or Solars. Now however Lunars have been brought up so often and so frequently, that It's getting to the point where I now consider Lunar to be a dirty word that immediately triggers a flash of irritation and contempt whenever I see it, regardless of the context.<br /> <br /> I don't mind Lunars in and of themselves, I think they have the potential to be interesting. I just wish their fans would shut up for a while.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yeah, that came out more aggressive than intended, as it's something I've been sitting on. No offense was meant, but I stand by it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 02-26-2015, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T18:06:52-08:00","id":420932,"title":"","content":"Honestly, you can reasonably tell the story of Creation with just the Solars and the Terrestrials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T18:27:57-08:00","id":420949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420908#post420908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I can understand how Lunar fans might feel that their favorite splat hasn't always gotten he best treatment. Heck, I can agree with it to some extent, and even go so far as to wish them the best of luck in the new edition.<br /> <br /> What I don't understand or sympathize with, is their incessant need to pollute the entire forum with Lunar threads, or turn every thread in to a Lunar thread, or bring up Lunars where they aren't even relevant to the discussion. I was, for the longest time, completely indifferent towards Lunars. I didn't dislike them, but they never appealed to me in any way like Sidereal, Infernals or Solars. Now however Lunars have been brought up so often and so frequently, that It's getting to the point where I now consider Lunar to be a dirty word that immediately triggers a flash of irritation and contempt whenever I see it, regardless of the context.<br /> <br /> I don't mind Lunars in and of themselves, I think they have the potential to be interesting. I just wish their fans would shut up for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can definitely see your position, I've felt some of that myself (especially with regard to the &quot;every thread is a Lunar thread&quot; meme being a reality). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420908#post420908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Yeah, that came out more aggressive than intended, as it's something I've been sitting on. No offense was meant, but I stand by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair, no worries!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T19:02:42-08:00","id":420976,"title":"","content":"Gayo's quote in your signature seems oddly appropriate at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T19:25:04-08:00","id":420989,"title":"","content":"I was a little confused by your vehemence against Lunars because I thought you were a fan.<br /> <br /> Then I realized I was getting you mixed up with Inugami.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T20:55:41-08:00","id":421170,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420843#post420843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, good Sol, I didn't actually expect people to have that wide a grade a response to what I said.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should end all my post with, &quot;And thus, such and such is better than Solars.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Cato the Elder and <i>Carthago delenda est</i>!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420932#post420932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, you can reasonably tell the story of Creation with just the Solars and the Terrestrials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feature, not a bug. There are way too many things in the game to for the typical narrative to work if you tried to throw every single one of them in at once, so the game doesn't try to force you to. This means that most Exalted have to, to some extent or another, feel &quot;optional.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Part of the problem that the Deathlords and, later, the post-Infernal Yozis had was that they started to feel too obligatory -- they were written in a way that meant that you either had to completely pretend that entire sections of their books didn't exist, or treat them as such a big deal that they washed out everything else. On its own this wouldn't have been so bad, but they were also tightly tied to their Exalted, especially the Infernals, which meant that if anyone wanted to play one you were often forced to bring the whole Reclamation baggage into your game unless everyone agreed to pretend that the first few chapters of Infernals never happened.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-27-2015, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T23:26:59-08:00","id":421369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=417903#post417903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The core concept wasn't the problem. The execution was left lacking by, from what we've heard, <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/troubled-lunar-history\" target=\"_blank\">hiring people who hated the concept, treating it with disdain, and injecting something else.</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting, hadn't read that before. Although I do recall Grabowski talking about how it suddenly hit him one day on the way to work that Lunars *should* be playable characters! I've always wanted to ask why they weren't to begin with. I mean, they were always an type of Exalted, why did it take so long to figure out that people would obviously want to play them? I sometimes wonder if the game would have been better if the original concept had been stuck with, but we've have gotten playable Lunars somewhere down the line, I'm sure.<br /> <br /> As to the mechanical problems of 2E Lunars, all I took away from the above is that this was Reason #341 Why Eclipse Charmshare Is A Serious Problem...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T06:38:16-08:00","id":421684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=421369#post421369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, hadn't read that before. Although I do recall Grabowski talking about how it suddenly hit him one day on the way to work that Lunars *should* be playable characters! I've always wanted to ask why they weren't to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>White Wolf has a history with &quot;Non-Player Splats&quot;. As I understand it, all cWoD-&quot;splats&quot; had one or more groups in them that weren't available to players... at least at the beginning, because sooner or later, I think most or all got splatbooks, too. So, I guess it was less &quot;There were Lunars, and there was a reason they were NPC-only&quot;, but actually &quot;Exalted needed an NPC-Splat, so they made Lunars (who then made the jump from NPC to PC during development)&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:24:01-08:00","id":422288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420708#post420708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Your point? I talked about that in my<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=418158#post418158\"> first post in this thread</a>, man.</div> </div> </div> </div>You claim that &quot;barbarian werewolves&quot; is too narrow and restricting an image for Lunars and that they need more variety. What I see is their dilution away from a powerful, evocative image to one of &quot;we are weird and glow silver because the moon&quot;. Adding too much to their themes just tears down the primal connotations they could so easily embrace. That lack of focus is what earned them the &quot;Silver Solars&quot; moniker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:28:30-08:00","id":422296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=421684#post421684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Wolf has a history with &quot;Non-Player Splats&quot;. As I understand it, all cWoD-&quot;splats&quot; had one or more groups in them that weren't available to players... at least at the beginning, because sooner or later, I think most or all got splatbooks, too. So, I guess it was less &quot;There were Lunars, and there was a reason they were NPC-only&quot;, but actually &quot;Exalted needed an NPC-Splat, so they made Lunars (who then made the jump from NPC to PC during development)&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly I think the jump was also a very 11th hour change timing wise as well. Poor Lunars.....<br /> <br /> I think part of it Hand of Omega was that the Lunars were conceptualized far more as a caricature specifically playing to being an NPC allies of the Fair Folk, marauding hordes. It's playing off a lot of information we never really got but I suspect it's safe to say the original NPC conception of Lunars wasn't a good premise for them as PC's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 02-27-2015, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T20:57:34-08:00","id":422574,"title":"","content":"Am I still in the dunce corner?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T03:59:19-08:00","id":422798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=422288#post422288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You claim that &quot;barbarian werewolves&quot; is too narrow and restricting an image for Lunars and that they need more variety. What I see is their dilution away from a powerful, evocative image to one of &quot;we are weird and glow silver because the moon&quot;. Adding too much to their themes just tears down the primal connotations they could so easily embrace. That lack of focus is what earned them the &quot;Silver Solars&quot; moniker.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite agree. All exalts should have some theme, but for PCs - especially in an Exalted game - this theme should not dominate your character options. For example, what would be the Solar image if you also tried to describe it in two words? I imagine &quot;Golden Heroes&quot; would be a typical image, but there are many Solars that are subtle rather than radiant and cunning or wise instead of traditionally heroic as per the ancient epic tales. They still have a powerful narrative because of their story - the ancient kings and masters, the corruption, betrayal, etc, etc. You can play the Radiant Kings Reborn game with Solars, but you don't have to - their previous edition skillset gave them plenty of other tools, and the new one will likely also give them many other options..Dragon-blooded are even more varied, and they are still both quite evocative and at least imo have plenty of good hooks. Has anyone ever complained how Dragon-blooded, who were created to serve the Solars and act as their intermediaries, have charms that allow them to rule? Yet there were probably no few cases in the First Age where a socially apt Lunar acted as the &quot;face&quot; of a reclusive Solar savant, or as the sage and occult advisor to their warlord mate.<br /> <br /> It is not about adding tons of themes, it is about having a theme sufficiently evocable to draw people in, yet wide enough to appeal to many niches. Lunar barbarians are definitely an iconic image, but that does not mean Lunar courtiers, poets, explorers, merchants, priests or generals should not exist or they can't come from urban or otherwise &quot;civilized&quot; cultures. Straight out of the box, Lunar shapeshifting is an awesome tool for infiltrators or masters of intrigue - just think of what shapeshifters in other settings have done without additional supernatural powers - and it's not like Luna or several generations of Lunars were too dumb come with the idea of blending in. In the First Age, they could try their hand in pretty much any area, even if the Solars had a guaranteed top spot. Lunars in the Age of Sorrows are often at the edges and affiliated with barbarian societies, because the Dragon-blooded and their Sidereal allies had been spending a lot of time and effort to keep them away up until very recently. That shouldn't mean Lunars want to be and have to be barbarians all the time, forever, period. They were nobles in the First Age, outcasts in the next one, and have the potential to be something else in the future. It would be quite weird for a splat that has transformation as a &quot;signature move&quot; if they had to be conceptually typecast, would it not?<br /> <br /> I wasn't here when the &quot;silver Solars&quot; nickname came up, but from what I hear Lunar fans were overall pretty happy at what the 2E Lunars were compared to the 1E ones, and most would much rather have the &quot;silver Solars&quot; than what came before. I would argue that it is the execution rather than the concept that was the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 02-28-2015, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T04:19:01-08:00","id":422805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=422798#post422798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't here when the &quot;silver Solars&quot; nickname came up, but from what I hear Lunar fans were overall pretty happy at what the 2E Lunars were compared to the 1E ones, and most would much rather have the &quot;silver Solars&quot; than what came before. I would argue that it is the execution rather than the concept that was the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my understanding, this may be a matter of 'that was not exactly a high bar to clear'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T06:34:14-08:00","id":422856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420256#post420256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only up to a certain point. If you try to grab from everything you could conceivably grab from you're gonna end up with a mess, <i>especially</i> with something that pulls in as many diverse directions as shapeshifters. One of the smartest things Geoff did in the 1e Lunars outline was attaching a separate file to the effect of &quot;Okay, before anyone starts writing, we all need to be on the same page about how Lunar shapeshifting works and what kind of shapeshifters Lunars are, because otherwise you're all going to run off with a bunch of contradictory ideas and assumptions and I will have a mess on my hands. Lunar shapeshifting is like this......&quot;<br /> <br /> (The 2e outline, notably, did not have any such thing-- and what followed was 8 years of people arguing about what kind of shapeshifters Lunars are.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping in mind that what Lunars in 1E were could be aptly summed up as &quot;sodding terrible&quot;, there is a decent argument that this was <i>still </i>better than the alternative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 02-28-2015, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T07:21:27-08:00","id":422890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=422805#post422805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From my understanding, this may be a matter of 'that was not exactly a high bar to clear'.</div> </div> </div> </div>And by and large, the writing for 2e didn't even make a proper attempt at going over it. It went to the side instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T10:20:52-08:00","id":423088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=422856#post422856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping in mind that what Lunars in 1E were could be aptly summed up as &quot;sodding terrible&quot;, there is a decent argument that this was <i>still </i>better than the alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problems Lunars had in 1e were (mostly) not a result of how shapeshifting worked, they were a result of it being written by people who had no idea how the genre they were writing worked and who were therefore terrible at making it look cool. It presented Lunars as dumb big strong barbarians (and gave them nothing but dumb big strong barbarian charms) because it was written by people who were picturing Ahnold from the 1982 Conan movie or Conan as imagined by Marvel comics rather than the original books.<br /> <br /> (Of course, there's also a lot of horrible stuff in the original Conan books in terms of the author's implicit beliefs about civilization and all that, but a well-written Lunars book can take that on the same way Solars take on the shiny golden hero motifs. The problem was that the 1e book was written by people who didn't understand what they were aiming for and therefore wrote a book based around playing a Ahnold as a meathead barbarian instead.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-28-2015, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T15:13:30-08:00","id":423484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=420989#post420989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was a little confused by your vehemence against Lunars because I thought you were a fan.<br /> <br /> Then I realized I was getting you mixed up with Inugami.</div> </div> </div> </div>*snicker, snicker*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T17:12:29-08:00","id":423576,"title":"","content":"You know what I liked about TAW? It made barbarians cool. I know that's shallow and subjective and silly, but that's my feels. It gave a niche to Lunars that they didn't have before, it gave them a reason to stand outside society beyond simply being contrary, and it held up a mirror to the all the ills and failings of what the current keepers of power called civilization.<br /> <br /> Forcing them to step side-ways also made the original idea of Solar wed to Lunar for political reasons a justifiable to fairly interesting thing, rather than something to shrug at or build weird mind control charms off of.<br /> <br /> Creation ruled by the Solar looks like the 1st Age (maybe, I could never decide if the First Age was a logical extension of giving 700 people waaaay too much power, or a super cynical look at a magic utopia, anyway!) Creation ruled by the Sidereal looks like the one that exists now, tragic and bearable and full of necessary compromise.<br /> <br /> We haven't seen what a world ruled by the Lunar looks like, and I think that's largely because the Lunar mindset doesn't preclude itself towards the building up of kingdoms. This is not to say they're not any good at it! (I admit I haven't thoroughly read or examined TAW, only skimmed it, if this is something it purported then I happily ignored it) Anyway, this is to say that the Lunar as a group have decided that they favor independence, that they think Creation does not need them to tell them what to do. It's an interesting story when all the other factions are seeking power in one way or another.<br /> <br /> So in my Creation/the one inspired by TAW, a lot more of the prodigies and incredible magic relics dotting the landscape of Creation are Lunar sourced. These just tend not to change history so much, because the Lunar make them or fight their battles or seduce their princes or princesses or whatever for their own reasons. Their power and legacy isn't as easily shared as that of Solar.<br /> <br /> And of course the Realm is going to be at odds with this, because any gigantic empire is going to be at odds with 300ish demigods going around doing whatever they want and flaunting their laws. Delicious conflict ensues.<br /> <br /> - - <br /> <br /> All this said, I hope 3rd Edition Lunars makes being a barbarian cool. Not to say that being a barbarian is the only thing a Lunar can do, but if they can make it interesting I think they'll have found an appropriate niche for the Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T17:23:41-08:00","id":423585,"title":"","content":"How do you define being a barbarian, though - someone opposed to &quot;civilization&quot; as per the Realms perspective, or just someone with a different idea of what civilization is? Lunar stereotypes have occasionally strayed a bit too much in the former category. I hope there may be plenty of ways for Lunars to be both, because both can allow for cool characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T17:45:49-08:00","id":423625,"title":"","content":"Lunar magic will be stylistically barbarian without forcing a Lunar to be the very image of &quot;barbarian&quot;.<br /> <br /> We know that Tattoos are still going to be a thing. There are also tattoo-artifacts.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping for a crafting Charm that represents a Lunar's talent at taking once-living materials like wood, bark, hair, skin and bone and turning them into useful tools... especially if they came from the corpse of someone or something you personally killed, and very especially also took their Heart's Blood. So you kill a tyrant lizard and fashion its jawbone into a massive hammer, a la <i>Monster Hunter</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm also hoping that if there's still a divide between true forms and false forms (Formlock is gone), that there will be a Charm that lets you wear the hide or feathers of a particular beast in order to treat that creature as a true form.<br /> <br /> Those are some examples of stylistic barbarianism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T23:09:19-08:00","id":423863,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:on-lunar-barbarism\" target=\"_blank\">Holden talks Lunars, barbarism, and barbarism's various definitions.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:06:58-08:00","id":424270,"title":"","content":"I got poked and told there was a thread that might involve me on the OP front page.<br /> <br /> I checked. Oh, it's a Lunar thread.<br /> <br /> Then I went and made a sandwich, walked the dog, had a nap, and tidied my desk, because <i>Lunar thread</i>. Successive poking has convinced to at least post <i>something</i>.<br /> <br /> To answer the most basic questions from the opening post - between TAW Lunars and 2e Lunars, TAW are probably the &quot;better&quot; shifters. They've got more Charms that interact with their shapeshifting, no form lock, no Tell, and more practical effects stemming from each form, and it's easier to homebrew new forms for them to take. On the other hand, 2e Lunars get their totem form for free, and have much more room for abusing shapeshifting at the extremes - mainly by taking a form with absurd Strength and giggling. Similarly, TAW probably have &quot;better&quot; Charms. They've got a wider variety of tricks, they were written at the end of the edition rather than its start, and many of their personal-scale Charms use the same sort of numbers as Solars. The main &quot;advantage&quot; 2e Lunars have in that contest is their overpowered soak and regen Charms, plus a few social tricks copypasted from Solars.<br /> <br /> The trickier question is the one about their differences in theme and focus. The two main issues are that 2e Lunars barely had any themes or focuses, while for most of its short history TAW was a grab-bag of whatever bit of eccentric homebrew a handful of fans had decided to do that week. A lot of its early missteps can be seen where &quot;unnerving outsider&quot; scrapes over the line into &quot;outright horror&quot;, which is more of the Abyssal or Infernal bailiwick - Lunar shapeshifting isn't, fundamentally, a biological process - the twisting of flesh and reconfiguring of bone is presumably something that <i>happens</i>, but it deliberately doesn't receive much focus. Pan and Lovecraft's Wilbur Whateley were both goat-legged chimeras, but their presentation was very different. This is what people tend to be talking about when they say &quot;Alex Mercer isn't a Lunar&quot; - his bag of tricks is a one-for-one match with what Lunars can do, but he's fundamentally a character of biological horror, which isn't what Lunars are for.<br /> <br /> So both 2e Lunars and TAW were nebulous clouds, separated mainly by vicious vicissitudes of the White Wolf forum shouting at itself, and even now it's difficult to know which version or interpretation of each is being referred to at any given time.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, there are paths to giving each a bit more definition. TAW is easy - it was trimmed into a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg\" target=\"_blank\">final version</a>, which cuts down on the verbiage and trims content unsuited to Lunar themes. It's much more coherent - and would have to be, as it's a single document put together with intent and purpose, rather than a drawing board covered in the graffiti and blueprints of a few people without so much as a Skype chat room to link them.<br /> <br /> 2e Lunars is harder, but still possible. It's best to approach it by looking at its history. 1e Lunars had a troubled development, essentially stemming from a clear (albeit last-minute) vision of barbarian adventures wrapped up in a werebeast package being handed over to writers who hated or didn't understand what they were asked to write. This resulted in a horrendous failure on almost every level. 2e Lunars, rather than trying to capture the original concept behind its predecessor, was written as a response to the execution of 1e Lunars, patching up or flinching away from the points where it had most obviously failed. To its credit, it was well-received on release - and remains one of the most playable early 2e splats, out of the box. Unfortunately, the cracks became more obvious as the edition progressed, especially when a few more mechanically interesting splats arrived. 1e Lunars had been a dreadful approach to a good idea, but in flinching away from its approach, 2e Lunars had also managed to put distance between itself and the good idea, and been left with little but &quot;animals and not like 1e&quot; to go on.<br /> <br /> I will acknowledge the obvious potential for bias on my part, but there's literally no character you can make as a 2e Lunar that you can't do better with a TAW Lunar. The opposite isn't true.<br /> <br /> A more interesting contrast, then, is between TAW and 3e Lunars.<br /> <br /> To put it in simple terms, as I see it:<br /> TAW was a response to 2e Lunars, just as 2e Lunars was a response to 1e Lunars.<br /> 3e Lunars are - or will be - an attempt to return to that original design pitch.<br /> <br /> In many places, they've hit on the same &quot;answers&quot; to Lunar problems in the setting. Both focus on &quot;Lunars vs The Empire&quot; as a major conflict, both try to make Lunar shapeshifting an interesting tool in itself, most of the previewed 3e Lunar effects work perfectly well in TAW (and, one suspects, vice-versa). It's no coincidence that the last time Holden and I disagreed about how Lunars should be portrayed, our disagreement came down to &quot;Lunars should be monsters, a category that includes witches&quot; vs &quot;Lunars should be witches, a category that includes monsters&quot;.<br /> <br /> In others, they've taken completely different tracks. As part of a whole new edition, 3e Lunars takes advantage of and introduces new setting conceits, while TAW was intended as a plug-in, and so mostly reinterpreted isolated chunks of setting rather than outright re-configuring the face of Lunars in Creation. I expect a greater degree of influence from Werewolf, which (for all that some fans seem allergic to it) isn't a bad thing - it's a question of properly incorporating it. 3e is embracing that point of inspiration, while TAW largely eschewed it (lumping less specific &quot;werewolf&quot; themes under the general &quot;skinwalker witch&quot; idea). 3e obviously works off very maximalist design precepts, which means it can make Lunar shapeshifting interesting the same way it tackled artifacts - unique and exciting powers for each animal, while TAW had to be self-contained and so produced a selection of general, adaptable &quot;animal traits&quot; that could be slapped onto a given form. Though both 3e and TAW are being written with a better understanding of what it means to be &quot;barbarian&quot; than previous editions, they'll probably have different approaches to this aspect of Lunars. TAW approached &quot;barbarian&quot; as a practical, in-setting result of the greater theme of &quot;outsider&quot;, while 3e Lunars will likely be tackling it directly, as a facet of primal Lunar power.<br /> <br /> At some point that shifted toward a general ramble, but hopefully you found it somewhat useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":605,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","user":"Revlid","date":". 03-01-2015, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","name":"Revlid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar605_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:43:37-08:00","id":424302,"title":"","content":"Heh, Revlid's post is #101.<br /> <br /> Edit: But seriously, am I ostracized still or what am I?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T11:55:35-08:00","id":424345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=424302#post424302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But seriously, am I ostracized still or what am I?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>I</i> never shunned you - no more so than normal anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:57:25-08:00","id":425427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=422798#post422798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't quite agree. All exalts should have some theme, but for PCs - especially in an Exalted game - this theme should not dominate your character options. For example, what would be the Solar image if you also tried to describe it in two words? I imagine &quot;Golden Heroes&quot; would be a typical image, but there are many Solars that are subtle rather than radiant and cunning or wise instead of traditionally heroic as per the ancient epic tales. They still have a powerful narrative because of their story - the ancient kings and masters, the corruption, betrayal, etc, etc. You can play the Radiant Kings Reborn game with Solars, but you don't have to - their previous edition skillset gave them plenty of other tools, and the new one will likely also give them many other options..Dragon-blooded are even more varied, and they are still both quite evocative and at least imo have plenty of good hooks. Has anyone ever complained how Dragon-blooded, who were created to serve the Solars and act as their intermediaries, have charms that allow them to rule? Yet there were probably no few cases in the First Age where a socially apt Lunar acted as the &quot;face&quot; of a reclusive Solar savant, or as the sage and occult advisor to their warlord mate.<br /> <br /> It is not about adding tons of themes, it is about having a theme sufficiently evocable to draw people in, yet wide enough to appeal to many niches. Lunar barbarians are definitely an iconic image, but that does not mean Lunar courtiers, poets, explorers, merchants, priests or generals should not exist or they can't come from urban or otherwise &quot;civilized&quot; cultures. Straight out of the box, Lunar shapeshifting is an awesome tool for infiltrators or masters of intrigue - just think of what shapeshifters in other settings have done without additional supernatural powers - and it's not like Luna or several generations of Lunars were too dumb come with the idea of blending in. In the First Age, they could try their hand in pretty much any area, even if the Solars had a guaranteed top spot. Lunars in the Age of Sorrows are often at the edges and affiliated with barbarian societies, because the Dragon-blooded and their Sidereal allies had been spending a lot of time and effort to keep them away up until very recently. That shouldn't mean Lunars want to be and have to be barbarians all the time, forever, period. They were nobles in the First Age, outcasts in the next one, and have the potential to be something else in the future. It would be quite weird for a splat that has transformation as a &quot;signature move&quot; if they had to be conceptually typecast, would it not?</div> </div> </div> </div>There have been many many real-life examples of &quot;barbarian&quot; explorers, poets, merchants, priests, and generals. Look at the Vikings - bloodthirsty raiders and one of the first cultures to have lawyers. &quot;Barbarianism&quot; is merely a theme and an approach. It comes with advantages and connotations, but no more so than Solars with their divine kingship and holy light. Lunars are instinctual, primal, self-reliant, passionate, predatory, willful, individualistic, and wild, even when being subtle and civilized. Just because a Lunar dons a silk dress and sips champagne at a court function doesn't mean that inside she has ceased to be a tiger. She just stalks a different jungle.<br /> <br /> They do not need to reject civilization, because civilization is a useful tool. However, tools can break. A Lunar with no tools will just make do without. Oddly, this reminds me of a quote from Halo. &quot;<i>When I joined the Corps, we didn't have any fancy-schmanzy tanks. We had sticks! Two sticks, and a rock for the whole platoon\u2014and we had to share the rock! Buck up, boy, you are one very lucky marine!</i>&quot; Sargent Johnson would make one hell of a Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:24:30-08:00","id":425539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=425427#post425427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because a Lunar dons a silk dress and sips champagne at a court function doesn't mean that inside she has ceased to be a tiger. She just stalks a different jungle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just got the image of Reacher Gilt from Going Postal as an urban Lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:05:33-08:00","id":425585,"title":"","content":"Should I try to better explain my Wrecking Witches position or is it too late for that now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T14:46:13-08:00","id":425700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=425427#post425427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There have been many many real-life examples of &quot;barbarian&quot; explorers, poets, merchants, priests, and generals. Look at the Vikings - bloodthirsty raiders and one of the first cultures to have lawyers. &quot;Barbarianism&quot; is merely a theme and an approach. It comes with advantages and connotations, but no more so than Solars with their divine kingship and holy light. Lunars are instinctual, primal, self-reliant, passionate, predatory, willful, individualistic, and wild, even when being subtle and civilized. <b>Just because a Lunar dons a silk dress and sips champagne at a court function doesn't mean that inside she has ceased to be a tiger. She just stalks a different jungle.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Gleaming shell of an outworn lie; fable of Right divine\u2014<br /> You gained your crowns by heritage, but Blood was the price of mine.<br /> The throne that I won by blood and sweat , by Crom, I will not sell<br /> For promise of valleys filled with gold, or threat of the Halls of Hell!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A wolf was no less a wolf because a whim of chance caused him to run with the watch-dogs.&quot;<br /> Robert E. Howard<br /> <br /> Since Conan kept on being brought up I think that his original author would agree with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T15:59:36-08:00","id":425744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=425585#post425585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should I try to better explain my Wrecking Witches position or is it too late for that now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Go ahead. No ones stopping you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T17:32:59-08:00","id":425824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=425700#post425700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Gleaming shell of an outworn lie; fable of Right divine\u2014<br /> You gained your crowns by heritage, but Blood was the price of mine.<br /> The throne that I won by blood and sweat , by Crom, I will not sell<br /> For promise of valleys filled with gold, or threat of the Halls of Hell!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A wolf was no less a wolf because a whim of chance caused him to run with the watch-dogs.&quot;<br /> Robert E. Howard<br /> <br /> Since Conan kept on being brought up I think that his original author would agree with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. I indulged in opening quotes for the three divisions of the TAW Storytelling section - Lunar Characters, Lunar Stories, and Other Exalts.<br /> <br /> They are, in order:<br /> \u201cIn this place I am a barbarian, because men do not understand me.\u201d - Ovid<br /> <br /> \u201cThe warm intimacies of small, kindly things, the sentiments and delicious trivialities that make up so much of civilized men's lives were meaningless to him. A wolf was no less a wolf because a whim of chance caused him to run with the watch-dogs.\u201d \u2013 Robert E. Howard<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you could only see the beast you've made of me<br /> I held it in but now it seems you've set it running free<br /> Screaming in the dark, I howl when we're apart<br /> drag my teeth across your chest to taste your beating heart\u201d \u2013 Florence + The Machine<br /> <br /> I'm pleased to see 3e's moving back to including such quotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","name":"Revlid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar605_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:37:21-08:00","id":426215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revlid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=425824#post425824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cIf you could only see the beast you've made of me<br /> I held it in but now it seems you've set it running free<br /> Screaming in the dark, I howl when we're apart<br /> drag my teeth across your chest to taste your beating heart\u201d \u2013 Florence + The Machine</div> </div> </div> </div>I've recently purchased a copy of the song titled &quot;Cage The Beast&quot; by Adelitas Way.<br /> <br /> <br /> I see it in your eyes,<br /> You're feeling paranoid,<br /> You know just what I've done,<br /> You know what I've <i>become</i>.<br /> <br /> I feel it deep inside,<br /> With all the pain and lies,<br /> I know just what I want,<br /> I am an <i>animal</i>.<br /> <br /> Well, I think it's time I let you know...<br /> (Why did you send me off?)<br /> <br /> You can't cage the beast!<br /> There's no breaking me!<br /> You can't cage the beast inside of me.<br /> I feel the rage!<br /> And all the the pain!<br /> You can't cage the beast inside of me.<br /> Inside of me.<br /> <br /> I feel it in your bite,<br /> You are a parasite,<br /> Who knows just what I've done.<br /> I think your time has <i>come!</i><br /> <br /> You try to turn the tide,<br /> I think you've lost your <i>mind!</i><br /> Afraid of what I want.<br /> This is what I've <i>become</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T14:55:57-08:00","id":428195,"title":"","content":"These are definitely a good inspiration, I meant that being a part of such a society is not really the defining part of a lunar, any more than being civilized is defining for a Solar or a Dragonblood. As for what Lunars have to be, well, it is an interesting topic. In a sense, is it not simply enough to be a capable (or lucky) enough mortal to catch the eye and grace of Luna, so that S/He can take you into its own? Your powers come with a theme and perhaps even a certain focus, but an exalted hero probably has their own personality and opinions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=425427#post425427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A Lunar with no tools will just make do without.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can certainly agree with that - in a sense this is how I see what happened to Lunars after the Usurpation. It's not that they really loved abandoning the remains of the greatest civilization ever built (not entirely without their work) and decided to reject all of this and go to the end of the world, it's that they had no choice and had to adapt.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 03-04-2015, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T16:06:33-08:00","id":428248,"title":"","content":"Slightly off topic, but I do have to say that my favorite part of TAW is the NPC's, and the seperation of NPC's by eras. I definatly prefer Ma Ha Suchi as a social genius than a strange goat thing. I also like the idea that the Deliberative Elders that were not ultra cautious and behind the scenes basically died off over time which leaves room for Shogunate and Realm &quot;Elders&quot;. Hopefully 3E will use that idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T05:56:32-07:00","id":435568,"title":"","content":"Is it fair to say that I thought how it handled some of the canonical elders was a bit of a cop out?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T06:27:44-07:00","id":435590,"title":"","content":"I don't see it but I certainly would like to hear why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:40:04-07:00","id":435689,"title":"","content":"Mostly how there's only really Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi left, Leviathan is probably dead and Lilith can barely be called a person.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T15:11:58-07:00","id":436322,"title":"","content":"Mm, that wasn't a copout exactly, that was a deliberate decision (by EarthScorpion, and I agree with it) to kill a chunk of the Lunar Elders.<br /> <br /> It was felt that the number of Lunar Elders held too much sway over the identity of Lunars as a splat, and that they constituted a setting problem because they were too powerful to be free actors, but unlike the Deathlords or similar figures they couldn't easily be shackled to a particular place to keep them from <i>being </i>free actors. Tamuz really should have more than just control over Chiarascuro, but when you've got around a dozen of these bozos floating around, each of which needs to have similar levels of accomplishment*, the setting starts to groan uncomfortably.<br /> <br /> That's part of why TAW has all those Shogunate- and early Realm-era Elders running around, violently disagreeing with the Deliberative-era Elders. They're a lot easier to fit into the setting, and it means people like Ma-Ha-Suchi or Raksi aren't alone in the spotlight as the face of What Lunars Become.<br /> <br /> Some of the dead Elders were pretty cool, like Tamuz**, so I can certainly see how you'd <i>disagree </i>with that decision, but I think calling it a copout is unfair.<br /> <br /> * Else they look like chumps, and that's unacceptable given the sway they held over the identity of Lunars as a splat.<br /> <br /> ** Although you could definitely re-introduce him as a Shogunate- or early Realm-era Elder with less of a firm grip over Chiaroscuro.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 03-10-2015, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T19:59:55-07:00","id":436591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=436322#post436322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mm, that wasn't a copout exactly, that was a deliberate decision (by EarthScorpion, and I agree with it) to kill a chunk of the Lunar Elders.<br /> <br /> It was felt that the number of Lunar Elders held too much sway over the identity of Lunars as a splat, and that they constituted a setting problem because they were too powerful to be free actors, but unlike the Deathlords or similar figures they couldn't easily be shackled to a particular place to keep them from <i>being </i>free actors. Tammuz really should have more than just control over Chiarascuro, but when you've got around a dozen of these bozos floating around, each of which needs to have similar levels of accomplishment*, the setting starts to groan uncomfortably.<br /> <br /> That's part of why TAW has all those Shogunate- and early Realm-era Elders running around, violently disagreeing with the Deliberative-era Elders. They're a lot easier to fit into the setting, and it means people like Ma-Ha-Suchi or Raksi aren't the face of the splat.<br /> <br /> Some of the dead Elders were pretty cool, like Tammuz**, so I can certainly see how you'd <i>disagree </i>with that decision, but I think calling it a copout is unfair.<br /> <br /> * Else they look like chumps, and that's unacceptable given the sway they held over the identity of Lunars as a splat.<br /> <br /> ** Although you could definitely re-introduce him as a Shogunate- or early Realm-era Elder with less of a firm grip over Chiaroscuro.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tamuz's* hold on Chiaroscuro was so tenuous from its popping into existence as a retcon that you could have easily ignored it and put him back in the wilderness; it really didn't have much to do with the Tri-Khan's political maneuvering, so it was quite irrelevant. Similarly, the other influence projects of the TSR didn't really hold much traction as &quot;super secret histories&quot;. Those places didn't have or need Lunar influence in their genesis back in Scavenger Sons, so trying to make them dependent on it is not going to work very well.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*One m. Two ms is the deceased Sidereal Tammiz Ushun.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T20:16:21-07:00","id":436609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=436591#post436591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tamuz's* hold on Chiaroscuro was so tenuous from its popping into existence as a retcon that you could have easily ignored it and put him back in the wilderness; it really didn't have much to do with the Tri-Khan's political maneuvering, so it was quite irrelevant. Similarly, the other influence projects of the TSR didn't really hold much traction as &quot;super secret histories&quot;. Those places didn't have or need Lunar influence in their genesis back in Scavenger Sons, so trying to make them dependent on it is not going to work very well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well <i>yeah</i>, it was a sop and I probably should've used the Haslanti League as an example instead, but Tamuz is still supposedly ruling from the shadows, while Arvida, not so much. Either works as an example; the point is canon Lunars have too many Elders running around making things difficult for the rest of us.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *One m. Two ms is the deceased Sidereal Tammiz Ushun. </div> </div> </div></span>Thanks, fixed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T09:19:08-07:00","id":437101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=436609#post436609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well <i>yeah</i>, it was a sop and I probably should've used the Haslanti League as an example instead, but Tamuz is still supposedly ruling from the shadows, while Arvida, not so much. Either works as an example; the point is canon Lunars have too many Elders running around making things difficult for the rest of us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. The example set by Arvida is more of &quot;if an elder tries to exert too much control, they die.&quot; Which fits with the whole Oz affair of 2e Lunars, really; built up, written as having absurd amounts of influence, but when you look behind that curtain...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T11:04:24-07:00","id":437237,"title":"","content":"Derp. I'm mixing Arvida up with Gerd Marrow-Eater... Who isn't a Deliberative Elder, apparently. Huh. I guess Tamuz was the right example to go for, but it's been ages since I read anything about canon Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 03-11-2015, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T20:49:44-07:00","id":437966,"title":"","content":"Although it's easy to see the temptation to kill off the Lunar elders (fitting them in is hard, definitely, and they're one of the big examples of Exalted's Elder Problem in general), I'd say it's a bad idea because having existing elders is one of the main ways the Lunar story differs from the Solar one. The hard part is to turn that into something interesting that can be usefully exploited for Lunar narratives, rather than making it feel like &quot;here are a bunch of people who got here before you did and did all the cool stuff first.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T14:13:54-07:00","id":438887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=437966#post437966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although it's easy to see the temptation to kill off the Lunar elders (fitting them in is hard, definitely, and they're one of the big examples of Exalted's Elder Problem in general), I'd say it's a bad idea because having existing elders is one of the main ways the Lunar story differs from the Solar one. The hard part is to turn that into something interesting that can be usefully exploited for Lunar narratives, rather than making it feel like &quot;here are a bunch of people who got here before you did and did all the cool stuff first.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes. That's another reason why TAW has a bunch of Shogunate- and early Realm-era Elders running around.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T07:20:04-07:00","id":439850,"title":"","content":"Less elderly elders and even younger elders. Them First Age elders with their visions of by-gone ages and power accrued over millennium too much for you? Well, most of them are dead or too insane to matter, but there are plenty more palatable options!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T13:20:49-07:00","id":440414,"title":"","content":"As far as the elder problem is concerned I don't see the world of difference between First Age and Shogunate era when it comes to the execution they're both older than the Imperial Calendar and occupy the general power threshold of &quot;whatever the Storyteller thinks is appropriate&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:36:03-07:00","id":440527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=440414#post440414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as the elder problem is concerned I don't see the world of difference between First Age and Shogunate era when it comes to the execution they're both older than the Imperial Calendar and occupy the general power threshold of &quot;whatever the Storyteller thinks is appropriate&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd probably be equal in power, but only First Age Elders ever saw Solars at their peak. Given that Exalted's setting <i>is</i> mostly Solar-centric, this could be a relevant difference... it creates Elder Lunars that don't get what all that &quot;Oh [no/yes], the Solars are back!&quot;-fuz First Age Elders give is all about. It creates Lunar Elders that can more readily underestimate Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:51:33-07:00","id":440537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=440527#post440527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'd probably be equal in power, but only First Age Elders ever saw Solars at their peak. Given that Exalted's setting <i>is</i> mostly Solar-centric, this could be a relevant difference... it creates Elder Lunars that don't get what all that &quot;Oh [no/yes], the Solars are back!&quot;-fuz First Age Elders give is all about. It creates Lunar Elders that can more readily underestimate Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the Lunar Elders are being written so that they can be boss fights for Solars, you need new Lunar Elders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:56:01-07:00","id":440544,"title":"","content":"It always felt to me that the Shogunate era never got the coverage it deserved. It's basically the middle step child between the first age and the present, ya know? Shogunate era Lunars help that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:57:17-07:00","id":440545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=440537#post440537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the Lunar Elders are being written so that they can be boss fights for Solars, you need new Lunar Elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said anything about boss fights? Solars change the world. First Age Elders of any kind of Exalt know that, and plan accordingly.<br /> A First Age Elder who think the return of the Solars doesn't matter is a fool. A Shogunate Lunar Elder, on the other hand, simply doesn't know better, and can be uncaring without comming accross as an idiot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T16:33:17-07:00","id":440588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=440414#post440414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as the elder problem is concerned I don't see the world of difference between First Age and Shogunate era when it comes to the execution they're both older than the Imperial Calendar and occupy the general power threshold of &quot;whatever the Storyteller thinks is appropriate&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a matter of outlook, more than anything. Power is also a concern, because while Shogunate-era Elders are mighty they aren't products of the Age of Dreams, greatest civilisation Creation has ever seen - but it's chiefly a matter of outlook. Having such a radical division between Lunar Elders is useful to dilute the power of figures like Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi as the 'face' of Lunars.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T17:20:22-07:00","id":440654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=440588#post440588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having such a radical division between Lunar Elders is useful to dilute the power of figures like Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi as the 'face' of Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty sad that Ma-Ha-Suchi (aka Ears) or Raksi would even be considered the face of Lunars in the first place, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Both of them, and Lunar elders in general tend to be fairly aloof and hard to get to, and they keep it this way. That's probably a big part of why they got to be elders and lived through a millenium and more of Dragon-blooded ascendancy - they were hard to find and kill. Both of them specifically shun the company of others and even limit that of their kind (to some degree). From a narrative point of view, they work much better as puppetmasters and hermit kings that you have to go through hell and back to get to. I think the Lunar narrative in general does not lend itself much to elders being the face of the bunch ,especiallz in the case of those two.<br /> <br /> I can see them as being representative of Lunars for us fans of the setting*, but in-character,there would probably be a hundred other lunars that are much more appropriate for characters to interact and bond with. Even for Lunar PCs, those two are not likely to be the most readily approachable. Compared to, say, the Sidereal book with a range of Sideareals of note from Chejop Kejak to relatively new agents of several hundred years, named Lunarstend to be rather ... unrepresentative of the overall range of the lot, and most make pretty poor companions. For many starting players, I think a lot of them are also simply rather unlikeable.<br /> <br /> *, which imo is pretty sad, because to me both are failures as Lunars - ironically, both prove quite unable to adapt to and match a different world, Ears as a bitter wreck trying to destroy what he once represented and Raksi as a stagnating genius girlchild shitting up a great wonder she did not create and even worse, has not shown any aptitude how to even use to gain greater power - that may be harsh but seriously, has she as a savant managed to do anything of note for however long she was in possession of one of the greatest depositories of knowledge of the First Age? Eldar Sidereals or Dragonblooded may be manipulative and unlikable jerks, but most are at least capable and competent jerks worthy of respect, and quite a few are easy to imagine getting behind and supporting.. Half of the Lunar Elders seem the sort of atavisms that you would rather simply put out to pasture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 03-13-2015, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T20:46:37-07:00","id":440832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=440588#post440588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a matter of outlook, more than anything. Power is also a concern, because while Shogunate-era Elders are mighty they aren't products of the Age of Dreams, greatest civilisation Creation has ever seen - but it's chiefly a matter of outlook. Having such a radical division between Lunar Elders is useful to dilute the power of figures like Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi as the 'face' of Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you wanted to dilute the power of figures like Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi as the 'face' of Lunars why are they the only Elders that survived from the First Age?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T06:16:34-07:00","id":441244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=440832#post440832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanted to dilute the power of figures like Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi as the 'face' of Lunars why are they the only Elders that survived from the First Age?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because just killing them <i>would</i> be a copout, at least from my perspective. Especially when they're the Elders who you can get the most use out of, both in play and in designing Lunars.<br /> <br /> Like it or not, they're influential figures on both Lunars and the playerbase. You can't just say, &quot;oh they're dead now, they don't matter anymore,&quot; when they have that much weight to them, you have to <i>counteract</i> them and the ideas they represent. Hence the opposing influence of the Moonkillers and Shogunate- or early Realm-era Elders, which casts the Deliberative-era Elders as one side in a divide in who Lunars are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T07:49:18-07:00","id":441298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=440527#post440527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'd probably be equal in power, but only First Age Elders ever saw Solars at their peak. Given that Exalted's setting <i>is</i> mostly Solar-centric, this could be a relevant difference... it creates Elder Lunars that don't get what all that &quot;Oh [no/yes], the Solars are back!&quot;-fuz First Age Elders give is all about. It creates Lunar Elders that can more readily underestimate Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this goes back to my problem with cutting the other First Age elders. Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi are easily the two who care the least about the return of the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> Obviously it's better than 2e Lilith and Leviathan who I'd struggle to use without one of the PCs being their mate, but there's a lot of middle ground here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 03-14-2015, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T09:11:16-07:00","id":441401,"title":"","content":"The approach of TAW to the First Age Elders was a direct response to 2e, where it seemed that every street corner held a several-thousand-year-old Celestial who knew everything about the ancient mysteries of the First Age and had a master plan to build a new, better utopia that'd be ready in just about five minutes, honest this time. Meanwhile, those hundreds of Lunars who'd presumably taken their Second Breath in the two thousand years <i>after </i>the Usurpation amounted to a handful of fresh new faces appropriate for starting PCs. This was particularly unsatisfactory in an edition where being an Elder meant everyone else got to bend over and take it, as it meant your First Age Lunar Elders were essentially Deathlords who weren't chained by secret weaknesses, ghostly insanity and the need for shadowlands. They were just supremely powerful NPCs who'd for some reason elected to fuck goats in the Wyld for two thousand years to build an army that was super-scary you guys because it had <i>horns</i> oh man wow Lookshy had better watch out.<br /> <br /> So, what TAW wanted was to make First Age Elders genuinely scary, while <i>also</i> restricting them to a plausible, gameable degree of influence over the setting. It also wanted to emphasize the real built-in long war nature of the Lunar/Realm conflict by spreading it across generation after generation, which would also fill the bizarre Shogunate-gap that ran through the setting.<br /> <br /> It <i>also</i> wanted to do this as briefly as possible, because it was intended to be a plug-in &quot;hack&quot; for Exalted games that would put little burden on Storytellers. Games could grab the mechanics wholesale or piecemeal, while the setting material worked without requiring any great attention to knock-on effects in the setting. It largely functions as an alternate look at the setting that games were already using - it examined it from different angles, took a different tone, and shifted the origins of certain events, but didn't actually change any non-Lunar setting elements.You could in theory slot it in without any problems - which made a detail-light take vital, one that would offer flexibility to Storytellers while also clearly defining the intended direction of the splat.<br /> <br /> Their numbers were cut down to make room for Shogunate (and even Realm-era) Elders, and to suggest risks on both sides - but more First Age Elders exist than those described in the TAW document. Raksi, Ma-Ha-Suchi, Lilith and (maybe) Leviathan were the ones that were detailed, but that's because each introduces a specific element of how TAW Elders work.<br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi demonstrates the long war. He's an insane Elder Monster who's crossed far too many lines, who showcases the callous use of &quot;barbarians&quot; as ammunition, and who may end up acting as your patron regardless. Raksi is an icon for the &quot;Guanxi&quot; dynamic that replaced the big campfire pow-wows that dominated the 2e Lunar &quot;community&quot;. She also shows off how a Lunar Elder might openly operate without interference. Leviathan's probably dead, but <i>by</i> being dead he exists as hype for the kind of setting impact Elder Lunars can have. This guy died before the Scarlet Empress took the throne, and pretty much the entire West is still terrified of him. Lilith's a look into the depths of the Lunar Great Curse, as well as a &quot;sympathetic&quot; First Age Lunar who touches on Solar relationships (without so much as mentioning Desus).<br /> <br /> The Shogunate Lunars are powerful and established, but they're not quite the insane Old Ones of the First Age. They've hit heights that you can reach in-game, so they might be different things you might aspire to. They show off how Lunars can be credible setting-actors in sub-Deathlord ways, as wandering adventurers and the lords of weird empires and enemies of the Sidereals. The Realm Lunars then exist as sig characters, each specifically showcasing a different game style described in the Storytelling chapter.<br /> <br /> Killing off most of the First Age Elders meant that the remainder could be built up as insane, terrifying monster-gods without needing to restrict them to playing Sim City with random mutants. One Ma-Ha-Suchi roaming the Realm and its satrapies like Randall Flagg crossed with Pan is <i>enough</i> to have an impact on how the Realm exists. One Leviathan making like Godzilla crossed with Nemo is <i>enough</i> to scar the collective memory of an entire direction. If Storytellers want to come up with their own Old Ones to fill out the reference to &quot;barely more than a handful&quot; still existing, these give them a ballpark to shoot for - mad witch-lords that warp worlds around them - and room to shoot for it. This focus on setting impact also makes them more gameable - most often, how many dice Ma-Ha-Suchi can throw at you isn't relevant, because you're dealing with the madness and hate he's stirred up rather than the creature himself.<br /> <br /> It also helps to retain the First Age's mystery - admittedly well-bludgeoned by that point - if your first-hand sources are few, far between, and totally unreliable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":605,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","user":"Revlid","date":". 03-14-2015, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","name":"Revlid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar605_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T10:49:34-07:00","id":441603,"title":"","content":"So problem is, therefore, &quot;I wanted you/thought you were going to shoot for <i>this</i>,&quot; when all along you were shooting for something else, making a lot of people feeling like you missed the mark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T13:05:46-07:00","id":441765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw?p=441603#post441603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So problem is, therefore, &quot;I wanted you/thought you were going to shoot for <i>this</i>,&quot; when all along you were shooting for something else, making a lot of people feeling like you missed the mark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm? What do you mean, specifically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","name":"Revlid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar605_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T20:01:36-07:00","id":442116,"title":"","content":"Well, I like TAW, but I get the impression that <i>other</i> people get the impression that you were going to do something more extensive, more retconning, shake foundations of the very setting so Lunars played a more prominent role. Something, I guess you're saying, would make it harder to easily plug it in.<br /> <br /> Whereas, instead, you did something more limited, to make transition into Creation easier","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}